    },
    "scoped_2026-06-11_why": "College-homonym subjects (Session 45, the CRIM M1003 case): the minority college's courses are a DIFFERENT department (ADM=police @ LATTC/MiraCosta vs graphics; AP=Anatomy&Physiology @ Modesto vs photography; PLS=Paralegal @ CCSF/SRJC vs plant science; OT=Occupational Therapy @ Grossmont; FS=Food Science @ Grossmont + Film Studies @ SBCC vs fire; GSS=social science @ Saddleback vs gunsmithing; IS=Global Studies/leadership/humanities, no CIS anywhere consistent; CADM=CAD @ Merced vs corrections; AET=ag equipment @ Butte; CAM=computer-aided mfg @ Fresno/Glendale vs culinary; AQUA=aquaculture @ Redwoods/SMC vs aquatics PE). Each is now a COLLEGE-SCOPED entry: the majority-side colleges keep the precise 0.8 fill; the minority side's stale fills retract on the next _infer_disciplines run and re-fill from per-row TOP/description/division evidence.",
    "audit_cleared": {
